    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is anchored by **James Wood** (78.42) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.75), who represent the highest-upside plays in the lineup. **James Wood** draws a favorable park factor and a generous matchup against a lefty, but his primary appeal is the stolen base opportunity against a slow pitcher, which boosts his efficiency rating significantly. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** is positioned in the two-hole with a massive platoon advantage that makes him a premier daily asset. **Corbin Carroll** (75.42) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (71.48) also remain elite starts; while **Corbin Carroll** is slightly hampered by an elite hold pitcher, his raw speed and order placement keep his floor exceptionally high, and **Tyler Soderstrom** continues to capitalize on favorable platoon matchups.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was leaving **Travis Bazzana** (51.16) on the bench. While his leadoff status provides a strong multiplier to his base projection, his individual efficiency metrics were eclipsed by the high-platoon and park-adjusted scores of our starting outfielders and middle infielders. Elsewhere, we are monitoring **Jose Caballero** (67.15) closely; he is an excellent start against a lefty, but he carries a 35% rain risk that could compromise his fantasy contribution if the game is shortened. Meanwhile, **Austin Riley** (51.24) remains in the lineup purely due to favorable wind conditions despite a tough matchup against a strong arm, proving the necessity of balancing pure talent against specific daily variables in our quest to maximize every category.",
